cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Joint Attainability of Worst-Case Co-expression Bounds via Capacitated Flows
message: >-
  If you use this code or the interval construction, please cite the accompanying
  paper and this repository.
authors:
  - given-names: Amy
    family-names: Wang
    affiliation: Massachusetts Institute of Technology
  - given-names: Manolis
    family-names: Kellis
    affiliation: Massachusetts Institute of Technology
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-04"
repository-code: "https://github.com/amywang2010/lr-certificates"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Per-contrast intervals for a co-expression score in spatial transcriptomics,
  valid over a declared set of molecule-to-cell reassignments (boundary-local
  reassignment with per-cell gain and loss capacity constraints, mask erosion and
  dilation, and a parameterised donor radius). Each interval end is a maximum flow
  on a signature-contracted cell network. A Hall criterion identifies when a
  per-transcript count already attains the flow value, and the maximum deficiency
  otherwise. A merged-network criterion decides in two further flows whether a
  single assignment attains both per-gene optima. A permutation null that
  recomputes the same worst-case object under every label permutation gives
  finite-sample-valid Monte Carlo p-values. A claim requires the interval to
  exclude zero and the matched null to confirm the direction. The selected
  one-sided p-value is doubled before Benjamini-Yekutieli correction, so direction
  selection is charged separately from dependence. Evaluated on three public
  Xenium sections spanning two tissues, two panel densities and two tumour types.
keywords:
  - spatial transcriptomics
  - molecule reassignment
  - matched permutation null
  - worst-case intervals
  - capacitated flow
  - Hall deficiency
  - selective inference
